nly period 201505).\n\n**Column concepts:**\n- **column_concept_assignable_area**: decision_guide — \"Assignable area statistics across a building's history records … Use FCLT_BUILDING_HIST.ASSIGNABLE_AREA\"; current building total → FCLT_BUILDING.ASSIGNABLE_AREA. All FCLT_* in m².\n- **column_concept_building_type_site**: decision_guide — \"Questions about current academic/residential buildings or buildings at a site (e.g. 'academic buildings at MIT'): Prefer FCLT_BUILDING.BUILDING_TYPE and FCLT_BUILDING.SITE: one row per building, no period duplication.\"\n- **column_concept_fiscal_period**: FCLT_BUILDING_HIST.FISCAL_PERIOD is the snapshot stamp for building history; use the history table's own FISCAL_PERIOD.\n\n**Concepts:**\n- **concept_building_inventory**: groups FCLT_BUILDING, FCLT_BUILDING_HIST(_1), FAC_BUILDING, BUILDINGS; decision guide confirms FCLT_BUILDING for current filters, FCLT_BUILDING_HIST for per-fiscal-period values.\n- **concept_room_space_inventory**, **concept_room_major_use_classification**, **concept_floor_inventory**: confirm FCLT_ROOMS is the FCLT-family room inventory with MAJOR_USE_DESC and AREA; FCLT_MAJOR_USE lists 'LABS'/'RESIDENT' as valid major-use descriptions.\n\n**Metrics (precedents):** dw_1888, dw_505, dw_1190, dw_126, dw_1488, dw_488, dw_1357, dw_385, dw_3332, dw_4061 etc. — full SQL retrieved for dw_1888/dw_505/dw_1190/dw_126; all use FCLT_BUILDING ⋈ FCLT_BUILDING_HIST on FCLT_BUILDING_KEY and FCLT_BUILDING ⋈ FCLT_ROOMS on FCLT_BUILDING_KEY, with filters `BUILDING_TYPE='ACADEMIC'`, `SITE='MIT'`, and Stata exclusion via `FCLT_BUILDING_KEY <> 32` (dw_1888).\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- `semantic_graph(query_neighbors, FCLT_BUILDING_HIST)`: joins — FCLT_BUILDING (incoming), FCLT_ROOMS, FCLT_FLOOR (outgoing); concept membership — concept_building_inventory; column_concepts — building_type_site, num_of_rooms, assignable_area, access_level, fiscal_period.\n- `semantic_graph(metrics_by_table, FCLT_ROOMS)`: 16 metrics consume FCLT_ROOMS (dw_4061, dw_1833, dw_3299, dw_1190, dw_1357, dw_1488, dw_1888, dw_3332, dw_3410, dw_488, dw_385, dw_3890, dw_4590, dw_4627, dw_1465, dw_4776) — heavy precedent for room-area aggregation joined to FCLT_BUILDING.\n- Hint join keys confirm: FCLT_BUILDING_HIST.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY ↔ FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY; FCLT_BUILDING.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY ↔ FCLT_BUILDING_HIST.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix** (building-source candidates):\n| Dimension | FCLT_BUILDING | FCLT_BUILDING_HIST | FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1 | FAC_BUILDING | BUILDINGS |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | 1 row/building (columns def) | 1 row/building/period (desc) | same as HIST (desc) | 1 row/building (desc) | 1 row/building (desc) |\n| Time coverage | current | 201505–201906 | 201505–201906 | current | current |\n| FISCAL_PERIOD column | absent (columns list) | present | present | absent | absent |\n| CAMPUS_SECTOR / EXT_GROSS_AREA | present | present | present | present | absent (only sq-ft measures) |\n| Key family | FCLT_BUILDING_KEY | FCLT_BUILDING_KEY | FCLT_BUILDING_KEY | FAC_BUILDING_KEY | BUILDING_KEY |\n| Fan-out risk | none | ×48 periods per building | ×48 | none | none |\n\nRoom-source candidates: FCLT_ROOMS (current, AREA m², MAJOR_USE_DESC — columns def) vs FCLT_ROOMS_HIST (only period 201505 — desc) vs FAC_ROOMS (FAC keys) vs SPACE_DETAIL (sq-ft, no major-use desc). \n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n- Required measure `SUM(room AREA)` filtered by MAJOR_USE_DESC IN ('RESIDENT','LABS'): FCLT_ROOMS SUPPORTED (columns AREA, MAJOR_USE_DESC); FCLT_ROOMS_HIST SUPPORTED structurally but coverage limited to 201505 (desc) — question needs all fiscal periods from building history; SPACE_DETAIL NOT-SUPPORTED (no major-use desc column).\n- Required `FISCAL_PERIOD` output: FCLT_BUILDING_HIST SUPPORTED; FCLT_BUILDING NOT-SUPPORTED (no FISCAL_PERIOD column in retrieved columns list).\n- Required `EXT_GROSS_AREA` output: hint maps to FCLT_BUILDING.EXT_GROSS_AREA — SUPPORTED (columns def: \"Extended gross area … in square meters\"). (FCLT_BUILDING_HIST also has EXT_GROSS_AREA, but hint explicitly anchors to FCLT_BUILDING.)\n- Required partition key `CAMPUS_SECTOR`: hint maps to FCLT_BUILDING.CAMPUS_SECTOR — SUPPORTED.\n- Filters BUILDING_TYPE='ACADEMIC', SITE='MIT', OWNERSHIP_TYPE='OWNED', key<>'32': FCLT_BUILDING SUPPORTED per column_concept_building_type_site decision_guide (\"academic buildings at MIT\" → prefer FCLT_BUILDING columns).\n- HAVING SUM(AREA) > 1000: SUPPORTED at building grain in FCLT_ROOMS⋈FCLT_BUILDING.\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:**\n- \"academic building at MIT … owned by MIT\" → FCLT_BUILDING.BUILDING_TYPE='ACADEMIC', SITE='MIT', OWNERSHIP_TYPE='OWNED' (domain-knowledge hints + decision_guide).\n- \"rooms used for 'RESIDENT' or 'LABS' purposes\" → FCLT_ROOMS.MAJOR_USE_DESC (hint mapping; FCLT_MAJOR_USE desc confirms these code descriptions exist).\n- \"fiscal period\" → FCLT_BUILDING_HIST.FISCAL_PERIOD (hint mapping).\n- \"running sum of assignable area within each campus sector\" → window SUM over FCLT_BUILDING_HIST.ASSIGNABLE_AREA partitioned by FCLT_BUILDING.CAMPUS_SECTOR (hint mapping).\n- \"external gross area\" → FCLT_BUILDING.EXT_GROSS_AREA (hint mapping).\n- \"not the Stata building\" → FCLT_BUILDING_KEY <> '32' (domain knowledge: Stata = building key '32'; dw_1888 precedent uses `FCLT_BUILDING_KEY <> 32`).\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:** FCLT_BUILDING⋈FCLT_BUILDING_HIST on FCLT_BUILDING_KEY: 4 precedents retrieved (dw_1888, dw_505, dw_1190, dw_126). FCLT_BUILDING⋈FCLT_ROOMS on FCLT_BUILDING_KEY with room-area aggregation: dw_1888, dw_488, dw_1190, dw_1465, dw_4061. Stata exclusion via key<>'32': dw_1888. Window over history rows: dw_126 (`MIN(...) OVER (PARTITION BY FCLT_BUILDING_KEY)`).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\nFCLT_BUILDING serves as the current classification dimension for all facility-space metrics (16 metrics on FCLT_ROOMS alone); FCLT_BUILDING_HIST serves fiscal-period trend/dispersion analysis (dw_505, dw_1190, dw_126, dw_1888); FCLT_ROOMS serves room-area statistics per building/use/organization. The question's shape (per-building room-area aggregate × per-period history attributes + window) matches the dw_126/dw_1888 pattern.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n- FCLT_BUILDING, FCLT_BUILDING_HIST, FCLT_ROOMS: semantic_get + semantic_graph (neighbors / metrics_by_table) ✓\n- FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1, FAC_BUILDING, FAC_ROOMS, FCLT_FLOOR(_HIST), FCLT_ROOMS_HIST, FCLT_MAJOR_USE(_HIST), BUILDINGS, SPACE_DETAIL/UNIT/USAGE/FLOOR, ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD, FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS(_HIST), FCLT_ORGANIZATION(_HIST), FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY, FAC_ORGANIZATION/MAJOR_USE/BUILDING_ADDRESS, TIME_MONTH/QUARTER/DAY, academic-domain tables (SUBJECT_*, SIS_*, etc. — discarded as unrelated to facilities task): examined via search descs + concept comparisons ✓\n- Concepts: concept_building_inventory (semantic_get) ✓; concept_room_space_inventory, concept_room_major_use_classification, concept_floor_inventory (search descs) ✓\n- Column concepts: assignable_area, building_type_site, fiscal_period (semantic_get) ✓; num_of_rooms, access_level, building_room (search descs + graph) ✓\n- Metrics: dw_1888, dw_505, dw_126, dw_1190 (semantic_get full SQL) ✓; dw_1488, dw_488, dw_1357, dw_385, dw_3332, dw_76, dw_565, dw_2596, dw_12 (search descs / metrics_by_table) ✓\n- mysql_query: attempted 6 times — all failed with \"Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'\" (infrastructure auth failure; data verification not possible this session).\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns**: FCLT_ROOMS (AREA, MAJOR_USE_DESC, FCLT_BUILDING_KEY) ⋈ FCLT_BUILDING (BUILDING_NAME, BUILDING_TYPE, SITE, OWNERSHIP_TYPE, CAMPUS_SECTOR, EXT_GROSS_AREA, FCLT_BUILDING_KEY) ⋈ FCLT_BUILDING_HIST (FISCAL_PERIOD, ASSIGNABLE_AREA).\n\n**6b. SQL approach**: (1) inner CTE aggregates room area per building with the RESIDENT/LABS + ACADEMIC + MIT + OWNED + key<>'32' filters and HAVING SUM(AREA)>1000 — aggregation at building grain before touching history avoids fan-out corruption of the HAVING threshold; (2) join the qualifying buildings to FCLT_BUILDING_HIST (1 row per building×period); (3) window `SUM(ASSIGNABLE_AREA) OVER (PARTITION BY CAMPUS_SECTOR ORDER BY FCLT_BUILDING_KEY, FISCAL_PERIOD ROWS UNBOUNDED PRECEDING)` following the hint's subquery-2/4 precedent; (4) select exactly: building name, fiscal period, total room area, running assignable area, ext gross area; order by fiscal period, building name. No rounding.\n\n**6c. Reasons**: *Data* — building-grain pre-aggregation prevents the ×48-period fan-out from inflating SUM(fr.AREA); FCLT_BUILDING_KEY is 1:1 with buildings (columns def). *Semantic-network* — decision guides explicitly route \"academic buildings at MIT\" filters to FCLT_BUILDING columns, fiscal-period values to FCLT_BUILDING_HIST, and history assignable-area windows to FCLT_BUILDING_HIST.ASSIGNABLE_AREA. *Business* — dw_126/dw_1888/dw_505 precedents use the identical join path and Stata exclusion; hint decomposition subqueries 1–4 map exactly onto this composition.\n\n**6d. Alternatives**: computing the running sum over the broader population (all academic/owned/non-Stata buildings, per hint subquery 2, before applying the room-area>1000 filter) is a possible reading; however, the question phrases all conditions as a single population (\"For each academic building … that has total area … > 1000, provide … the running sum\"), so the running sum is computed over the qualifying buildings, consistent with the composite-question convention. The DB auth failure prevented empirical tie-breaking; the hint decomposition (subquery 4 = subquery 2 + EXT_GROSS_AREA, then combined with subquery-1 filters) supports the single-population reading.\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
